  "subject": {
    "id": "governed-object-event-population",
    "type": "DOCUMENT"
  },
  "summary": "Admit Event and EventParticipation records under a declared ontology role.",
  "why": "P9 was deferred on 2026-09-03 and built on 2026-09-04 under the overnight relay instruction, not because a consumer earned it. compile_population_plan now admits the events family only when the bound domain-history profile declares an Event ontology role, and event_participations only when the compiled contract also carries the EventParticipation type; every other case still refuses with FAMILY_NOT_ADMITTED. CREATE_EVENT_PARTICIPATION stages participation without widening relation endpoints. Two facts are recorded rather than hidden: 13f11aa restored the canonical operation dependency order after the new family disturbed it with no preceding failing test, and 2f9bb90 pins that order afterwards instead. Event-to-Event ordering and Signal population remain unimplemented."
}
